(\cite{EP}) An unstable $A$-module $M$ is called nil-closed if:
\begin{center}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $M$ is reduced.
    \item $Ker(Sq_{1})=Im(Sq_{0})$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{center}

Let $E$ be an unstable $\mathrm{H}^{\ast}V-A$-module such that:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  $E$ is free as an $\mathrm{H}^{*}V$-module.
    \item  $\overline{E}$ is reduced as unstable $A$-module.
\end{enumerate}
Then $E$ is reduced as unstable $A$-module.
